# SD
1. Policyholder is a physical and environmental object.
2. Claims Adjuster is a physical and systemic object.
3. Client Portal is an informatical and systemic object.
4. Claims System is an informatical and systemic object.
5. Vehicle is a physical and environmental object.
6. Insurance Policy is an informatical and systemic object.
7. Insurance Policy is stateful.
8. Claim is an informatical and systemic object.
9. Claim is stateful.
10. Payment Order is an informatical and systemic object.
11. Decision Letter is an informatical and systemic object.
12. Payment System is an informatical and systemic object.
13. Claim Handling is an informatical and systemic process.
14. Claims Adjuster and Policyholder handle Claim Handling.
15. Claim Handling requires Claims System, Client Portal, Insurance Policy, Payment System, and Vehicle.
16. Claim Handling yields Claim, Decision Letter, and Payment Order.
# SD1
1. Claim Handling from SD zooms in SD1 into Claim Reporting, Claim Registering, Damage Assessing, Claim Deciding, Indemnity Paying, and Policyholder Notifying, which occur in that time sequence.
2. Claims Adjuster is a physical and systemic object.
3. Policyholder is a physical and environmental object.
4. Client Portal is an informatical and systemic object.
5. Claims System is an informatical and systemic object.
6. Payment System is an informatical and systemic object.
7. Vehicle is a physical and environmental object.
8. Insurance Policy is an informatical and systemic object.
9. Insurance Policy can be invalid or valid.
10. Decision Letter is an informatical and systemic object.
11. Payment Order is an informatical and systemic object.
12. Claim is an informatical and systemic object.
13. Claim can be approved, assessed, paid, registered, rejected or reported.
    State paid is final.
    State reported is initial.
14. Damage Description is an informatical and systemic object.
15. Photo Set is an informatical and systemic object.
16. Indemnity Amount of Claim is an informatical and systemic object.
17. Claim consists of Damage Description and Photo Set.
18. Claim exhibits Indemnity Amount.
19. Claim Handling is an informatical and systemic process.
20. Claim Reporting is an informatical and systemic process.
21. Policyholder handles Claim Reporting.
22. Claim Reporting requires Client Portal.
23. Claim Reporting yields Claim.
24. Claim Reporting invokes Claim Registering.
25. Claim Registering is an informatical and systemic process.
26. Claim Registering changes Claim from reported to registered.
27. Claim Registering requires Claims System and Insurance Policy at state valid.
28. Damage Assessing is an informatical and systemic process.
29. Damage Assessing changes Claim from registered to assessed.
30. Claims Adjuster handles Damage Assessing.
31. Damage Assessing requires Claims System and Vehicle.
32. Damage Assessing affects Indemnity Amount of Claim.
33. Claim Deciding is an informatical and systemic process.
34. Claims Adjuster handles Claim Deciding.
35. Claim Deciding requires Claims System, Indemnity Amount of Claim, and Insurance Policy.
36. Indemnity Paying is an informatical and systemic process.
37. Indemnity Paying occurs if Claim is approved, in which case Indemnity Paying changes Claim from approved to paid, otherwise Indemnity Paying is skipped.
38. Indemnity Paying requires Indemnity Amount of Claim and Payment System.
39. Indemnity Paying yields Payment Order.
40. Policyholder Notifying is an informatical and systemic process.
41. Policyholder Notifying requires Claims System and Client Portal.
42. Policyholder Notifying yields Decision Letter.
43. Claim Deciding changes Claim from assessed to exactly one of approved or rejected.
